---

<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="60–70 minutes" data-extension-duration="15–20 minutes">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Vocabulary and discourse · Lesson 19</p>
  <h1>Discourse linkers: <em>show the relationship, then build the argument</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">A linker is a small instruction to the listener or reader. It can announce a reason, turn toward a contrast, introduce evidence, or show that a conclusion follows. The linker cannot create logic that is missing. First decide how two ideas are related. Then choose a structure, punctuation pattern, and level of formality that make that relationship easy to follow.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">60–70 min core</span>
    <span class="tag">reason · result · contrast · example</span>
    <span class="tag">clause · phrase · punctuation · register</span>
    <span class="tag">15–20 min listening and retrieval</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Recover the relationship between ideas before naming a linker.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Choose clause, phrase, and sentence-connector patterns accurately.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Test</b><span>Check whether the evidence really supports the connection.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Communicate</b><span>Deliver and defend a connected recommendation.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line"><b>Can-do:</b> By the end, you can connect ideas through addition, contrast, concession, reason, result, example, clarification, sequence, and conclusion; choose between a conjunction, a dependent-clause linker, a phrase linker, and a sentence connector; punctuate high-value patterns; place <span class="ex">also</span> naturally; distinguish neutral conversation from more formal proposal language; make important relationships audible through chunking and stress; reject a connector when the logic is unsupported; and give a 90-second fictional recommendation that another person can reconstruct and challenge.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You recovered a cause, a contrast, a completed sequence, and a natural project collocation from prerequisite lessons.">
    <h3>Reactivate familiar connections</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Discourse foundation choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="because the last bus had already left">because the last bus had already left</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="but the evening route is more direct">but the evening route is more direct</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="First compare the routes; then recommend one">First compare the routes; then recommend one</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="made a recommendation based on the report">made a recommendation based on the report</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="although because the route">although because the route</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Maya took a taxi <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="because the last bus had already left" data-hint="The missing words must introduce the cause of the taxi decision." data-fix="Maya took a taxi because the last bus had already left.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The daytime bus is cheaper, <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="but the evening route is more direct" data-hint="The second clause contrasts one advantage with a different advantage." data-fix="The daytime bus is cheaper, but the evening route is more direct.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The tutor wants a process with comparison before judgment: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="First compare the routes; then recommend one" data-hint="Choose the option that makes the two stages and their order explicit." data-fix="First compare the routes; then recommend one.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The committee studied the evidence and then <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="made a recommendation based on the report" data-hint="Retrieve make a recommendation and connect it to its evidence source." data-fix="The committee made a recommendation based on the report.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice the instructions inside a connected recommendation</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Fictional Riverbend evening-access proposal</h3>
    <p><b>Disconnected notes:</b> Evening classes end at 9:30. The last direct bus leaves at 9:20. Some learners leave class early. A shuttle would cost money. A trial could test demand. The committee recommends a trial.</p>
    <p><b>Connected version:</b> Some learners leave class early <span class="ex">because</span> the last direct bus leaves before evening classes end. <span class="ex">However</span>, a permanent shuttle would require a large commitment. <span class="ex">For example</span>, the center would need to pay for a vehicle, a driver, and accessible boarding. <span class="ex">Although</span> the initial survey is limited, it identifies a transport concern worth testing. <span class="ex">Therefore</span>, the committee recommends a 12-week trial rather than a permanent service.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which word introduces the cause of early departure?</li>
      <li>Which connector turns from the access problem to a cost concern?</li>
      <li>Which expression introduces concrete parts of the cost?</li>
      <li>Which linker admits a limitation before preserving the main point?</li>
      <li>Which connector presents the recommendation as a result of the preceding reasoning?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You recovered the reason, contrast, example, concession, and result from the complete recommendation.">
    <h3>Discovery check: name what each linker tells the listener</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Riverbend linker choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="because">because</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="However">However</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="For example">For example</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Although">Although</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Therefore">Therefore</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Meanwhile">Meanwhile</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The sentence uses <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="because" data-hint="Look for the word immediately before the cause: the bus leaves too early." data-fix="Because introduces the cause of some learners leaving early.">choose</button> to explain why some learners leave early.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The writer uses <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="However" data-hint="The text turns from a transport problem toward a disadvantage of the solution." data-fix="However introduces the contrasting cost concern.">choose</button> to turn toward the cost concern.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The list of vehicle, driver, and boarding costs begins with <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="For example" data-hint="The list illustrates the general claim that a shuttle requires money." data-fix="For example introduces concrete instances of the cost.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The writer uses <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Although" data-hint="The dependent clause admits the survey limitation before the main clause states its value." data-fix="Although introduces the conceded limitation.">choose</button> to concede that the survey is limited.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The final recommendation begins with <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Therefore" data-hint="The writer presents a limited trial as the consequence of the access evidence and cost concern." data-fix="Therefore signals the reasoned result.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Get to the root: decide the relationship before the linker</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Linkers make relationships explicit. They do not make unrelated ideas logical, and they do not replace evidence. Before choosing a word, state the relationship in plain language: <span class="ex">this is another reason</span>, <span class="ex">this conflicts with the expectation</span>, <span class="ex">this cause produced that result</span>, or <span class="ex">this specific case illustrates the general claim</span>. Then choose a pattern that fits the grammar and the situation.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>communicative job</th><th>high-value B1 choices</th><th>relationship</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>addition</td><td><span class="ex">and · also · too · in addition · moreover</span></td><td>adds a new supporting point</td></tr>
      <tr><td>contrast</td><td><span class="ex">but · however · while · whereas · though</span></td><td>shows a meaningful difference or changed direction</td></tr>
      <tr><td>concession</td><td><span class="ex">although · even though · despite · in spite of</span></td><td>admits one fact while maintaining another point</td></tr>
      <tr><td>reason</td><td><span class="ex">because · because of</span></td><td>introduces a cause or explanation</td></tr>
      <tr><td>result</td><td><span class="ex">so · therefore · as a result</span></td><td>introduces a consequence supported by the cause</td></tr>
      <tr><td>example or clarification</td><td><span class="ex">for example · such as · in other words</span></td><td>illustrates a claim or restates it more clearly</td></tr>
      <tr><td>sequence or conclusion</td><td><span class="ex">first · next · meanwhile · finally · overall · in conclusion</span></td><td>organizes stages or closes the complete line of thought</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line"><b>Important boundary:</b> More linkers do not automatically create better writing or speaking. Repeat a noun, use a pronoun, or begin a clear new sentence when the relationship is already obvious. A connector should reduce the listener’s work, not decorate every sentence.</p>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You classified each relationship from its meaning rather than from a memorized connector list.">
    <h3>Classify the relationship before choosing wording</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Logical relationship choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="addition">addition</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="contrast">contrast</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="concession">concession</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="reason">reason</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="result">result</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="example or clarification">example or clarification</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="unrelated decoration">unrelated decoration</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The first study room is quiet. The second supporting point is that it has reliable internet. This relationship is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="addition" data-hint="The second point gives another benefit without reversing the first." data-fix="Another supporting benefit expresses addition.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The train is cheaper. The bus, by comparison, is faster. This relationship is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="contrast" data-hint="The speaker compares different advantages of two options." data-fix="Different advantages create a contrast.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The survey is small. The committee still believes a trial is useful. Admitting the first fact while maintaining the second is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="concession" data-hint="The first fact weakens but does not cancel the main position." data-fix="Admitting a limitation while preserving the main point is concession.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The class moved online. The instructor was sick and could not travel. The second idea supplies the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="reason" data-hint="It explains why the class moved online." data-fix="The instructor’s illness is the reason for the change.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The road flooded overnight. Morning buses were canceled. The cancellation is the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="result" data-hint="The flooding caused the later cancellation." data-fix="The cancellation is the result of the flooding.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The center offers practical support. Free résumé reviews illustrate that general claim. Their relationship is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="example or clarification" data-hint="The specific service shows what practical support includes." data-fix="Free résumé reviews are an example of practical support.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Choose the structure: clause, phrase, or new sentence</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>structure</th><th>safe pattern</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>coordinating conjunction</td><td>clause <span class="ex">, but / so</span> clause</td><td><span class="ex">The route is longer, but it is more reliable.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>dependent clause</td><td><span class="ex">because / although</span> + subject + verb</td><td><span class="ex">Although the route is longer, it is more reliable.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>preposition phrase</td><td><span class="ex">because of / despite</span> + noun or <span class="ex">-ing</span> form</td><td><span class="ex">Despite the longer route, the bus arrives earlier.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>sentence connector</td><td>Sentence. <span class="ex">However / Therefore / For example,</span> sentence.</td><td><span class="ex">The route is longer. However, it is more reliable.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>When the dependent clause comes first, a comma normally separates it from the main clause: <span class="ex">Because the last bus leaves early, some learners miss the final activity.</span> When the reason comes second, the comma is normally unnecessary: <span class="ex">Some learners leave early because the last bus leaves at 9:20.</span> For a B1 writer, a period before <span class="ex">however</span> or <span class="ex">therefore</span> is a clear, dependable choice. Formal edited writing can also use a semicolon before the connector.</p>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You matched because and although with clauses, because of and despite with noun phrases, but inside one sentence, and however between sentences.">
    <h3>Complete the exact grammatical frame</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Linker structure choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="because the direct bus leaves at 9:20">because the direct bus leaves at 9:20</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="because of the early departure time">because of the early departure time</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Although the response rate was limited">Although the response rate was limited</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Despite the limited response rate">Despite the limited response rate</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="but it serves more neighborhoods">but it serves more neighborhoods</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="However, it serves more neighborhoods">However, it serves more neighborhoods</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="because of the bus leaves">because of the bus leaves</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Use <span class="ex">because</span> before a full clause: Some learners leave early <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="because the direct bus leaves at 9:20" data-hint="After because, include the subject the direct bus and the verb leaves." data-fix="Some learners leave early because the direct bus leaves at 9:20.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Use <span class="ex">because of</span> before a noun phrase: Attendance may be affected <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="because of the early departure time" data-hint="Because of takes the noun phrase the early departure time." data-fix="Attendance may be affected because of the early departure time.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Begin with a concession clause containing a subject and verb: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Although the response rate was limited" data-hint="Choose although plus the complete clause the response rate was limited." data-fix="Although the response rate was limited, the survey identified a concern.">choose</button>, the survey identified a concern.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Begin with a concession phrase rather than a clause: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Despite the limited response rate" data-hint="Despite takes the noun phrase the limited response rate." data-fix="Despite the limited response rate, the survey identified a concern.">choose</button>, the survey identified a concern.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Keep the contrast inside one sentence after a comma: The route costs more, <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="but it serves more neighborhoods" data-hint="But is the coordinating conjunction that joins the second full clause here." data-fix="The route costs more, but it serves more neighborhoods.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Begin a new sentence with a punctuated connector: The route costs more. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="However, it serves more neighborhoods" data-hint="Choose the capitalized sentence connector followed by a comma." data-fix="The route costs more. However, it serves more neighborhoods.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Keep cause, result, and concession in one complete frame</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Standard edited English normally uses one frame for each relationship. Choose <span class="ex">because</span> or <span class="ex">so</span>, not both in the same cause-result pair: <span class="ex">Because the bus was late, we took a taxi.</span> Or: <span class="ex">The bus was late, so we took a taxi.</span> Choose <span class="ex">although</span> or <span class="ex">but</span>, not both: <span class="ex">Although it costs more, it saves time.</span> Or: <span class="ex">It costs more, but it saves time.</span></p>
  <p><span class="ex">Even though</span> often makes the concession feel stronger than <span class="ex">although</span>. <span class="ex">Despite</span> and <span class="ex">in spite of</span> express a similar relationship, but they take a noun phrase or an <span class="ex">-ing</span> form: <span class="ex">Despite costing more, the direct route remains popular.</span></p>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You selected one complete cause, result, or concession frame and avoided double linking.">
    <h3>Choose the requested relationship and sentence shape</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Cause result concession choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Because the workshop ends after the last bus, some learners leave early">Because the workshop ends after the last bus, some learners leave early</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="The workshop ends after the last bus, so some learners leave early">The workshop ends after the last bus, so some learners leave early</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="The workshop ends after the last bus. As a result, some learners leave early">The workshop ends after the last bus. As a result, some learners leave early</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Although the shuttle costs more, it provides a later option">Although the shuttle costs more, it provides a later option</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Despite the additional cost, the shuttle provides a later option">Despite the additional cost, the shuttle provides a later option</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Because the workshop ends late, so learners leave early">Because the workshop ends late, so learners leave early</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Use a fronted reason clause, then a main clause: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Because the workshop ends after the last bus, some learners leave early" data-hint="Choose because plus a complete cause clause, followed directly by the result clause." data-fix="Because the workshop ends after the last bus, some learners leave early.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Put the cause first and join the result with <span class="ex">so</span> inside one sentence: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="The workshop ends after the last bus, so some learners leave early" data-hint="The requested frame is cause, comma plus so, result." data-fix="The workshop ends after the last bus, so some learners leave early.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Put the result in a new sentence beginning with a connector: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="The workshop ends after the last bus. As a result, some learners leave early" data-hint="Choose the two-sentence version with As a result followed by a comma." data-fix="The workshop ends after the last bus. As a result, some learners leave early.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Concede the full clause <span class="ex">the shuttle costs more</span>: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Although the shuttle costs more, it provides a later option" data-hint="Although takes the full subject-verb clause the shuttle costs more." data-fix="Although the shuttle costs more, it provides a later option.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Concede the noun phrase <span class="ex">the additional cost</span>: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Despite the additional cost, the shuttle provides a later option" data-hint="Despite takes a noun phrase rather than a full subject-verb clause." data-fix="Despite the additional cost, the shuttle provides a later option.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Place addition, contrast, examples, and conclusions naturally</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>choice</th><th>position and setting</th><th>natural model</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">also</span></td><td>usually before a main verb; after <span class="ex">be</span>; after the first auxiliary</td><td><span class="ex">It also serves Oak Street. It is also accessible. It can also run later.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">too</span></td><td>often at the end in neutral conversation</td><td><span class="ex">The later route serves Oak Street, too.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">in addition / moreover</span></td><td>sentence connectors; <span class="ex">moreover</span> is more formal and less common in relaxed speech</td><td><span class="ex">The route is direct. In addition, it runs later.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">though</span></td><td>often at the end in conversation to add a softer contrast</td><td><span class="ex">The express bus is faster. It costs more, though.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">for example / such as</span></td><td><span class="ex">for example</span> can introduce a sentence; <span class="ex">such as</span> introduces examples inside a noun phrase</td><td><span class="ex">Some costs increased. For example, fuel rose 8%. Costs such as fuel and insurance increased.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">overall / in conclusion</span></td><td>closes the whole discussion; it does not mean the same as a logical result</td><td><span class="ex">Overall, a limited trial is the most defensible next step.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You placed also naturally, matched formal and conversational contrast, distinguished sentence examples from noun-phrase examples, and closed the whole recommendation.">
    <h3>Match wording to position, channel, and purpose</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Placement and register choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="also serves Oak Street">also serves Oak Street</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is also wheelchair accessible">is also wheelchair accessible</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Moreover, the proposed service includes two evening departures">Moreover, the proposed service includes two evening departures</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="It is faster, though">It is faster, though</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="For example, 47 respondents reported leaving early">For example, 47 respondents reported leaving early</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Overall, a limited trial is the most defensible next step">Overall, a limited trial is the most defensible next step</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="serves also Oak Street">serves also Oak Street</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Put <span class="ex">also</span> before the main verb: The proposed shuttle <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="also serves Oak Street" data-hint="Before the main verb serves is the neutral position for also." data-fix="The proposed shuttle also serves Oak Street.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Put <span class="ex">also</span> after <span class="ex">be</span>: The proposed vehicle <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is also wheelchair accessible" data-hint="With be, place also after is." data-fix="The proposed vehicle is also wheelchair accessible.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Add a second supporting detail in a formal written proposal: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Moreover, the proposed service includes two evening departures" data-hint="Choose the formal sentence connector that adds another supporting feature." data-fix="Moreover, the proposed service includes two evening departures.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Add a relaxed spoken contrast after admitting the express bus costs more: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="It is faster, though" data-hint="In conversation, final though can add a softer contrasting advantage." data-fix="It is faster, though.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Illustrate the survey concern with one exact finding: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="For example, 47 respondents reported leaving early" data-hint="Choose the connector that introduces a concrete instance of the general concern." data-fix="For example, 47 respondents reported leaving early.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Close the complete comparison without pretending the last sentence is a physical consequence: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Overall, a limited trial is the most defensible next step" data-hint="Overall summarizes the judgment after considering the full discussion." data-fix="Overall, a limited trial is the most defensible next step.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Audit the logic before polishing the sentence</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Ask five questions: Are both ideas clear? What exact relationship joins them? Does the first idea actually support the second? Is the connector appropriate for the channel and tone? Does the punctuation match the structure? If the evidence is weak, change the claim or add evidence. Do not hide the gap behind <span class="ex">therefore</span>.</p>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>A connector cannot rescue a weak relationship</h3>
    <p><b>Unsupported:</b> <span class="ex">The trial begins Monday. Therefore, every participant will find a job.</span> The date does not prove the employment outcome.</p>
    <p><b>Supported and limited:</b> <span class="ex">The trial begins Monday. Therefore, the center can start collecting attendance and feedback next week.</span> The planned start supports the stated next action.</p>
    <p><b>Repetition disguised as addition:</b> <span class="ex">The route is inexpensive. Moreover, it does not cost much.</span> The second sentence restates the first without adding support.</p>
    <p><b>Example mismatch:</b> <span class="ex">Several transport options run after 10:00. For example, the library closes at 8:00.</span> The library schedule does not illustrate the transport claim.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You identified unsupported inference, useful result, empty repetition, relevant example, and accurate contrast from the supplied evidence.">
    <h3>Diagnose the relationship, not only the grammar</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Logical audit choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="unsupported inference">unsupported inference</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="supported result">supported result</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="repetition without a new point">repetition without a new point</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="relevant example">relevant example</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="accurate contrast">accurate contrast</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="punctuation alone proves the claim">punctuation alone proves the claim</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><span class="ex">Twenty people attended one workshop. Therefore, the course permanently improved all participants’ careers.</span> This is an <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="unsupported inference" data-hint="Attendance does not establish permanent career change or an outcome for every participant." data-fix="The connector presents a conclusion that the attendance evidence cannot support.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span><span class="ex">The driver reported a mechanical problem. As a result, the 9:35 departure was canceled.</span> With the report confirmed, this is a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="supported result" data-hint="The confirmed mechanical problem directly explains the canceled departure." data-fix="The cancellation is a supported result of the reported mechanical problem.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span><span class="ex">The shuttle is affordable. Moreover, its price is not high.</span> This is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="repetition without a new point" data-hint="The second sentence repeats the cost judgment instead of adding a different reason." data-fix="Moreover needs a genuinely new supporting point here.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span><span class="ex">Several services could improve evening access. For example, an on-demand shuttle could connect the center to the late train.</span> This is a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="relevant example" data-hint="The specific shuttle is one member of the general category of evening-access services." data-fix="The on-demand shuttle is a relevant example of an evening-access service.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span><span class="ex">The fixed route is cheaper, whereas the on-demand service reaches more neighborhoods.</span> This is an <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="accurate contrast" data-hint="The sentence compares different advantages of two named options." data-fix="Whereas accurately contrasts the cheaper fixed route with the wider on-demand service.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Sound natural: make the relationship audible</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Sentence connectors often form a short opening chunk. Pause after the connector, then give the main information its strongest stress: <span class="ex">howEVer, / the LAST bus leaves at NINE twenty.</span> <span class="ex">For exAMple, / forty-SEVen respondents left EARly.</span> <span class="ex">As a reSULT, / the committee proposed a TRIAL.</span> The pause helps the listener prepare for the relationship; it is not a full stop that disconnects the connector from its sentence.</p>
  <p>Conjunctions usually stay inside the clause rhythm. In relaxed U.S. speech, <span class="ex">and</span> can reduce toward /ən/ and <span class="ex">because</span> often sounds like /bɪˈkəz/: <span class="ex">It is CHEAPer / ən it runs LATEr.</span> <span class="ex">They left EARly / because the LAST bus was at NINE twenty.</span> Do not erase the key relationship word when clarity depends on it.</p>
  <p>Final <span class="ex">though</span> often carries a small separate beat and a continuing contrast: <span class="ex">It costs MORE. / It is FASter, though.</span> In a correction, the connector itself can receive stronger stress: <span class="ex">I agree with the GOAL. howEVer, / the current plan is too EXPENsive.</span></p>
  <section data-lesson-extension="Tutor-read connector chunking, reduced conjunctions, contrast stress, final though, and cause-result listening check">
    <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You heard opening connector chunks, integrated conjunctions, contrastive stress, final though, and the difference between cause and result.">
      <h3>Tutor-read listening: recover the relationship from rhythm and wording</h3>
      <p class="note-line">The tutor reads each line once naturally and once with the target chunking emphasized. The learner answers before rereading the written line.</p>
      <div class="quiz-list">
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="However forms an opening chunk, and the main information receives the later strong stress." data-hint="Listen for the short pause after however and the stronger content words in the main sentence." data-fix="However forms an opening chunk; the later clause carries the main information."><p class="quiz-question">1. Tutor line: “howEVer, / the LAST bus leaves at NINE twenty.” What does the chunking do?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="However forms an opening chunk, and the main information receives the later strong stress.">However forms an opening chunk, and the main information receives the later strong stress.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="However becomes the subject of the verb leaves.">However becomes the subject of the verb leaves.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The pause removes every contrast from the sentence.">The pause removes every contrast from the sentence.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="And is reduced inside one flowing addition, while the content words carry the important stress." data-hint="Listen to the lighter and between the two service benefits." data-fix="Reduced and links one flowing addition; cheaper and later carry the information stress."><p class="quiz-question">2. Tutor line: “It is CHEAPer / ən it runs LATEr.” What happened to <span class="ex">and</span>?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="And is reduced inside one flowing addition, while the content words carry the important stress.">And is reduced inside one flowing addition, while the content words carry the important stress.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="And is deleted from the grammar and becomes however.">And is deleted from the grammar and becomes however.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Every sound in and receives the strongest stress.">Every sound in and receives the strongest stress.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The stronger stress on however highlights a correction or important turn." data-hint="The speaker accepts the goal, then emphasizes a disagreement with the current plan." data-fix="Strong stress on however makes the corrective turn especially important."><p class="quiz-question">3. Tutor line: “I agree with the GOAL. howEVer, / the current plan is too EXPENsive.” Why is <span class="ex">however</span> prominent?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The stronger stress on however highlights a correction or important turn.">The stronger stress on however highlights a correction or important turn.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The speaker has forgotten the contrast and is listing identical facts.">The speaker has forgotten the contrast and is listing identical facts.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="However always requires the loudest stress in every sentence.">However always requires the loudest stress in every sentence.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Final though adds a conversational contrast to the earlier cost disadvantage." data-hint="The second sentence preserves a faster-service advantage after the cost concern." data-fix="Final though adds a conversational contrast: it costs more, but it is faster."><p class="quiz-question">4. Tutor line: “It costs MORE. / It is FASter, though.” What is the job of final <span class="ex">though</span>?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Final though adds a conversational contrast to the earlier cost disadvantage.">Final though adds a conversational contrast to the earlier cost disadvantage.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Though proves that the cost and speed are physically identical.">Though proves that the cost and speed are physically identical.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Though introduces the reason the vehicle exists.">Though introduces the reason the vehicle exists.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Because introduces the early bus as the cause; as a result introduces the early departure as the consequence." data-hint="Track which fact explains and which fact follows." data-fix="Because points to the cause, while as a result points to the consequence."><p class="quiz-question">5. Tutor lines: “They left early because the last bus was at 9:20.” “The last bus was at 9:20. As a result, they left early.” What stays the same?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Because introduces the early bus as the cause; as a result introduces the early departure as the consequence.">Because introduces the early bus as the cause; as a result introduces the early departure as the consequence.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Both expressions introduce an unrelated example about ticket prices.">Both expressions introduce an unrelated example about ticket prices.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The second version reverses which event happened and why.">The second version reverses which event happened and why.</button></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <h2>Read a complete proposal before judging its conclusion</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Fictional Riverbend evening-access file</h3>
    <p><b>Current situation:</b> Evening workshops end at 9:30, but the last direct bus leaves at 9:20. In an optional survey, 120 of 190 registered learners responded. Forty-seven respondents said they had left at least one workshop early during the previous month because of transport timing.</p>
    <p><b>Proposed trial:</b> Therefore, the access committee proposes a 12-week shuttle trial with departures at 9:35 and 10:15. The quoted total is $7,200. Moreover, the contract requires a wheelchair-accessible vehicle, a clearly marked pickup point, and driver contact information.</p>
    <p><b>Limits and concerns:</b> However, the survey records self-reports from respondents, not observed behavior from all 190 learners. It does not show how many people would use the shuttle. For example, some respondents may already carpool or use a different bus. Although the responses identify a timing concern, they do not prove that the trial will increase attendance or improve later employment outcomes.</p>
    <p><b>Recommendation:</b> Overall, the committee recommends a limited trial rather than a permanent service. During the trial, the center should record ridership, on-time departures, accessibility problems, cost per trip, and anonymous reports of leaving early. At week 12, the committee can compare those measures with the previous 12 weeks and decide whether to continue, revise, or stop the service.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You followed the transport contrast, proposal, accessibility addition, evidence limits, and measurable conclusion without letting the connectors overstate the file.">
    <h3>Evidence check: reconstruct the connected argument</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Workshops end ten minutes after the last direct bus leaves." data-hint="Compare the 9:30 workshop ending with the 9:20 direct-bus departure." data-fix="Workshops end at 9:30, ten minutes after the last direct bus leaves at 9:20."><p class="quiz-question">1. What timing contrast motivates the proposal?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Workshops end ten minutes after the last direct bus leaves.">Workshops end ten minutes after the last direct bus leaves.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The direct bus leaves ten minutes after every workshop ends.">The direct bus leaves ten minutes after every workshop ends.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The file gives no workshop or bus time.">The file gives no workshop or bus time.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="It presents the 12-week trial as a response to the stated access concern, not as proof of future success." data-hint="Separate the reason for proposing a test from evidence about an outcome that has not happened." data-fix="Therefore links the access concern to a limited trial proposal; it does not prove the trial’s future success."><p class="quiz-question">2. What does <span class="ex">Therefore</span> do in the proposed-trial paragraph?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It presents the 12-week trial as a response to the stated access concern, not as proof of future success.">It presents the 12-week trial as a response to the stated access concern, not as proof of future success.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It proves that every registered learner will use the shuttle.">It proves that every registered learner will use the shuttle.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It introduces an unrelated example about the library.">It introduces an unrelated example about the library.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The contract adds an accessible vehicle, a marked pickup point, and driver contact information." data-hint="Read the items introduced as an additional contract feature after moreover." data-fix="Moreover adds the accessible vehicle, marked pickup point, and driver contact information."><p class="quiz-question">3. Which supporting detail is added with <span class="ex">Moreover</span>?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The contract adds an accessible vehicle, a marked pickup point, and driver contact information.">The contract adds an accessible vehicle, a marked pickup point, and driver contact information.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The contract removes every accessibility requirement.">The contract removes every accessibility requirement.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The survey observed all 190 learners using a shuttle.">The survey observed all 190 learners using a shuttle.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The survey is optional self-report evidence from 120 respondents and does not establish actual shuttle use or later outcomes." data-hint="Preserve the response count, evidence type, and the two outcome limits stated in the file." data-fix="The optional survey reports 120 respondents’ experiences; it does not establish actual trial use, attendance change, or later employment outcomes."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which sentence accurately states the survey’s evidence limit?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The survey is optional self-report evidence from 120 respondents and does not establish actual shuttle use or later outcomes.">The survey is optional self-report evidence from 120 respondents and does not establish actual shuttle use or later outcomes.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The survey directly observed all 190 learners and proved permanent career improvement.">The survey directly observed all 190 learners and proved permanent career improvement.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Because the survey is limited, none of its responses can identify a transport concern.">Because the survey is limited, none of its responses can identify a transport concern.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Run a limited trial, measure use, reliability, access, cost, and early departure, then compare and decide." data-hint="Choose the conclusion that includes a limited action, relevant measures, a comparison, and a later decision." data-fix="The file recommends a 12-week trial with defined measures, comparison, and a continue-revise-stop decision."><p class="quiz-question">5. Which summary preserves the logic of the overall recommendation?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Run a limited trial, measure use, reliability, access, cost, and early departure, then compare and decide.">Run a limited trial, measure use, reliability, access, cost, and early departure, then compare and decide.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Make the service permanent now because one survey proves every future benefit.">Make the service permanent now because one survey proves every future benefit.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Ignore transport timing because limited evidence can never support a test.">Ignore transport timing because limited evidence can never support a test.</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build a concession and a measured conclusion</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="although the survey is limited it identifies a concern worth testing" data-hint="Begin with Although the survey is limited, then state what the survey still identifies." data-fix="Although the survey is limited, it identifies a concern worth testing." data-success-message="Correct. The although-clause concedes the evidence limit, and the main clause preserves the survey’s narrower value.">
    <h3>Builder 1: concede without abandoning the evidence</h3><p class="tile-target">Build the complete sentence.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="worth">worth</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="survey">survey</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="it">it</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="Although">Although</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="concern">concern</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="limited">limited</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="testing">testing</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="identifies">identifies</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="a">a</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="is">is</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="therefore the committee recommends a limited trial with defined measures" data-hint="Begin with Therefore, name the committee and recommendation, then add the trial limit and measurement condition." data-fix="Therefore, the committee recommends a limited trial with defined measures." data-success-message="Correct. Therefore introduces a measured recommendation that follows from the concern and the evidence limits.">
    <h3>Builder 2: state a supported result</h3><p class="tile-target">Build the complete sentence.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="defined">defined</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="committee">committee</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="with">with</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="Therefore">Therefore</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="trial">trial</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="measures">measures</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="limited">limited</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="a">a</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="recommends">recommends</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair the linker frame</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="but" data-hint="Although already introduces the concession frame, so do not add a second contrast conjunction." data-fix="Although the survey is limited, it identifies a concern. / The survey is limited, but it identifies a concern." data-why="Although plus a dependent clause and but plus coordinated clauses are alternative contrast frames in standard edited English." data-success-message="Correct. Removing but leaves one complete although-concession frame.">
    <h3>Repair 1: remove the double contrast</h3><p>Tap the extra linker.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="although">Although</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="survey">the survey is limited,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="but">but</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="concern">it identifies a concern.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="because of" data-hint="A full clause follows: the workshop ends. Use because directly before a subject and verb." data-fix="The shuttle is useful because the workshop ends after the last direct bus." data-why="Because introduces the full clause the workshop ends; because of would require a noun phrase such as the late workshop ending." data-success-message="Correct. Because now introduces the full subject-verb reason clause.">
    <h3>Repair 2: distinguish a clause from a noun phrase</h3><p>Tap the phrase with the wrong structure.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="shuttle">The shuttle is useful</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="because of">because of</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="workshop">the workshop ends</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="bus">after the last direct bus.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="however" data-hint="However is a sentence connector here, not a coordinating conjunction like but." data-fix="The trial is short. However, the committee will collect five relevant measures." data-why="A comma alone should not join two independent clauses with however. A period before and comma after the connector creates a clear B1 pattern." data-success-message="Correct. However now begins a properly punctuated sentence-connector chunk.">
    <h3>Repair 3: punctuate the sentence connector</h3><p>Tap the connector that cannot follow only a comma in this sentence.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="trial">The trial is short,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="however">however</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="committee">the committee will collect</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="measures">five relevant measures.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Practice a connected position without disclosing private information</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>You never need to discuss a real employer, commute, disability, financial problem, immigration matter, school record, family conflict, or unsafe travel experience. Use Riverbend, another tutor-created community proposal, or an invented choice. The purpose is discourse control, not evaluation of your private circumstances.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Relationship cards:</b> The tutor says <span class="ex">addition, contrast, concession, reason, result, example, clarification, sequence</span>, or <span class="ex">conclusion</span>. Give one sentence pair from the fictional file and state why the relationship fits.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Register switch:</b> Give a relaxed spoken version with <span class="ex">but, too</span>, or final <span class="ex">though</span>. Then give a neutral-formal written version with <span class="ex">however, in addition</span>, or <span class="ex">overall</span>. Keep the relationship and evidence unchanged.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Evidence challenge:</b> Your partner says <span class="ex">Therefore</span> before an unsupported conclusion. Ask what evidence connects the ideas, then reformulate the claim with a narrower result or a clear limitation.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>One-minute edit:</b> Take six disconnected notes. Group related ideas, remove one unnecessary linker, add one missing relationship, and explain each remaining choice.</div>

  <h2>Final production and check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: deliver and defend a 90-second fictional recommendation</h3>
    <p>Use the Riverbend file or another tutor-supplied proposal. State the issue and desired decision. Give two reasons, add one different supporting point, and illustrate one claim with a relevant example. Contrast two options. Concede one real limitation without abandoning the entire argument. Present one result that the evidence actually supports. Close with a measured recommendation. Use at least one conjunction, one dependent-clause linker, and one sentence connector. After your partner challenges a weak connection, clarify or reformulate it instead of adding a decorative connector.</p>
    <p><b>Success criteria:</b> Can the listener label each relationship, recover the evidence behind the conclusion, hear the connector chunks, identify the register, and explain the final action without finding a double linker, comma splice, irrelevant example, repeated point, or unsupported result?</p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You preserved reason-result direction, clause and phrase structure, connector punctuation, register, evidence limits, and spoken chunking across a complete B1 recommendation.">
    <h3>Final check: defend every connection</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The last direct bus leaves before class ends, so some learners leave early." data-hint="Put the cause first, then introduce its supported result with so." data-fix="The last direct bus leaves before class ends, so some learners leave early."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which sentence presents the bus timing as the cause and early departure as its result?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The last direct bus leaves before class ends, so some learners leave early.">The last direct bus leaves before class ends, so some learners leave early.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Some learners leave early, although the bus therefore.">Some learners leave early, although the bus therefore.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Because the bus leaves early, so the committee however.">Because the bus leaves early, so the committee however.</button></div></div>
